        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: घट्टः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "घट्टः — ghaṭṭaḥ — \"a bathing ghat; river steps\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्रातः घट्टे यात्रिकाः स्नान्ति। prātaḥ ghaṭṭe yātrikāḥ snānti. In the morning pilgrims bathe at the bathing ghat."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "घट्टः (ghaṭṭaḥ) is the word MW gives for a landing-place, a bathing place or steps by a river, with no derivation; CDIAL notes that a Dravidian origin has been suggested (T. Burrow), so its origin is uncertain; it lives on as Hindi ghāṭ, \"a bathing or landing place\" (MW; CDIAL 4414)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
